# Loaded by `npm run build`. Inlined into the bundle at build time, so changing
# this is a rebuild, not a restart.

# The deployed mock server, called directly — no proxy in front of it. It answers
# on 4000, not 80, and every response already carries
# `access-control-allow-origin: *`, so the cross-origin call works.
#
# No trailing slash: client.ts appends paths that begin with one.
VITE_API_BASE=http://localhost:4000

# If the built SPA is ever served over HTTPS, a browser will block every one of
# these calls as mixed content — an http:// API cannot be reached from an
# https:// page. That needs TLS on the API (or a same-origin proxy in front of
# it), at which point set this to `/api` and let the proxy do the stripping, as
# deploy/nginx.conf.template already does.
